NEARS-1067 AC4 (THE RISKY ONE) — sale expiry collapses the top slot back to banner-top with NO reload.

METHOD (no DB write — hard project rule respected): a local rewriting proxy on :8010 forwarded
every request to a real `php artisan serve` on :8011, rewriting ONLY the /api/v1/flash-sales
`end_date` to now+40s. The app (already pointed at 10.0.2.2:8010) therefore received a genuine
API response whose sale expires on-screen. DB untouched; seeded sale still ends 2026-07-15.

GROCERY HOME — observed vertical order (uiautomator, y = top edge):
  T+0    RAIL@y=720   countdown ['00','00','00','31']
  T+18s  RAIL@y=720   countdown ['00','00','00','19']
  T+25s  RAIL@y=720   countdown ['00','00','00','10']
  T+32s  (rail gone)
  ...stable through T+60s

POST-EXPIRY LAYOUT (same screen, no reload, no re-navigation):
  y=  717-1293  LIMITED OFFER / Fresh Mart Grocery / Claim Deal   <- BANNER now occupies the TOP slot
  y= 1476-1560  Categories
  'Flash Sale' occurrences: 0    <- rail did not strand, and did not stick as a shimmer

NETWORK: exactly 1 x GET /api/v1/flash-sales for the whole window
  => the collapse was purely reactive (the tick-side emit fires BEFORE the timer cancel);
     a reload would have shown a 2nd GET.
LOGS: clean (no [ERR]/[FAIL]/EXCEPTION).
